---
import Legal from '../../layouts/Legal.astro';
const EMAIL = 'tyler@btso.dev';
---
<Legal
  pageTitle="Privacy Policy | Dispatch: Email Templates & Digests for Jira"
  heading="Dispatch privacy"
  description="What Dispatch stores inside your Jira site, what it never collects, and how data is deleted."
  lastUpdated="November 24, 2026"
>
  <p>
    This policy covers Dispatch: Email Templates &amp; Digests for Jira ("Dispatch"), a Jira Cloud
    app distributed through the Atlassian Marketplace. Dispatch is provided by Brandon South
    (btso.dev, <a href={`mailto:${EMAIL}`}>{EMAIL}</a>). Effective date: November 24, 2026.
  </p>

  <h2>Runs on Atlassian</h2>
  <p>
    Dispatch is built entirely on Atlassian Forge and runs inside Atlassian's infrastructure. We do
    not operate any external servers, we use no third-party subprocessors, and the app declares no
    external network permissions (its <code>permissions.external</code> list is empty), so Dispatch
    cannot send your data outside Atlassian. We, the vendor, have no access to your Jira data.
  </p>

  <h2>What Dispatch stores</h2>
  <p>
    Dispatch stores the following in Atlassian Forge storage, scoped to your Jira site:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Templates:</b> the email templates your admins create or edit.</li>
    <li><b>Notification rules:</b> projects, events, conditions, recipients (Jira account IDs, group
      IDs and their display names) and delivery settings.</li>
    <li><b>Pending digest entries:</b> temporary items waiting for the next hourly or daily digest,
      such as issue key, summary, change details and permitted comment excerpts. They are deleted
      after delivery, or dropped after at most 3 delivery attempts.</li>
    <li><b>Delivery log:</b> the most recent 200 delivery records, with the rule, issue, status,
      recipients by account ID and display name, and the reason anyone was left out. Older records
      are removed automatically.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Email addresses</h2>
  <p>
    Dispatch never accesses or stores user email addresses. Notifications are delivered through
    Jira's native notification API using Jira account IDs, and Jira itself resolves where to send
    the email.
  </p>

  <h2>Restricted comments</h2>
  <p>
    Comments restricted to a role or group, and Jira Service Management internal notes, are never
    included in email and never stored in digest excerpts. Excerpts are re-checked before a digest
    is sent.
  </p>

  <h2>What we don't do</h2>
  <p>
    We do not sell or share your information, show advertisements, use analytics or tracking, or
    copy your Jira data to any system outside Atlassian.
  </p>

  <h2>Retention and deletion</h2>
  <p>
    Jira admins can delete templates and rules and clear the delivery log at any time inside the
    app. When you uninstall Dispatch, its access to your site ends immediately and Atlassian deletes
    the app's Forge storage according to Atlassian's Forge data retention policy.
  </p>

  <h2>Atlassian</h2>
  <p>
    Atlassian hosts and processes app data under its own terms and
    <a href="https://www.atlassian.com/legal/privacy-policy">privacy policy</a>. Billing and license
    data for Dispatch are handled by Atlassian Marketplace.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes and contact</h2>
  <p>
    If this policy changes, the date at the top of this page will be updated. Questions can be sent
    to <a href={`mailto:${EMAIL}`}>{EMAIL}</a>.
  </p>
</Legal>
